From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:13:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 25/30] drama: the tower's one decode row attends as a
 thread-block cluster

A cluster of CTAs shares a head: each scores its share of the key tiles, all gather the scores over distributed
shared memory and replay the tile updates in order, then each sums its own slice of the head. Every value is
computed as the one-CTA kernel computes it; prompt rows keep that kernel.
---
 zig/kernels/cuda/drama_tower.cu  | 134 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 zig/src/families/drama/tower.zig |   6 +-
 2 files changed, 139 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

